      "id": 1,
      "text": "Pocopson Township was incorporated on September 13, 1849, carved from Pennsbury, Thornbury, and Upper Oxford townships, and named after a Lenape term meaning “smoky place” along Pocopson Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Pocopson_Township,_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A covered bridge built in 1857 and the 1870 Wilmington and Northern Railroad spurred businesses at Pocopson Station, turning it into a local hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Pocopson_Township,_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
